    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** standing as the clear offensive anchor. With a score of 79.39, he benefits from a premier leadoff spot against King and a significant platoon edge that inflates his value in our scarcity-heavy model. While we prioritize speed, **Trea Turner** (53.63) provides a solid floor despite facing a formidable opponent in Sale; his elite sprint speed and leadoff placement remain indispensable, even against a high-end lefty. Conversely, **Yordan Alvarez** (49.34) faces a tough matchup against Smith, where the L/L platoon disadvantage and a strong opposing xERA drag his score down, though his elite 0.442 xwOBA prevents a total benching.\n\nOur middle-infield rotation shows lower volatility today, with **Pedro Ramirez** (48.29) and **Chase Meidroth** (43.69) hovering in the marginal category. **Caleb Durbin** (40.92) remains in the lineup due to thin alternatives, though he faces the steepest climb today against Schlittler\u2019s sharp 2.94 xERA. The decision to start this group was made while navigating the unfortunate reality that key contributors like **Junior Caminero**, **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** are completely unavailable due to league-wide off-days. With **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** also lacking viable matchups or game availability, our bench remains largely inactive. The primary risk today lies in the top of the order; if King navigates the early innings efficiently, the production from **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Pedro Ramirez** could be stunted, potentially forcing a defensive shell move to preserve our remaining game caps.",
